# Milestone: M3
# Covers: closure capture from definition scope, not call scope; 'var Object.f'
#         slot assignment on a prototype; lookup of i inside f() resolves to
#         outer global i, not inner block-local i.
# blocked: requires mutable Object proto (UPROTO_READONLY); var Object.f fails with TypeError — v1.0-rc
# matrix-row: object-slot-install
#
# Reason:
#   'var Object.f = function(x) { i += x }' assigns a function to a slot on the
#   Object prototype — requires M4 prototype-OOP slot write dispatch.  At M3, var
#   declarations are local to the current compilation unit (no prototype slots).
#   The core closure-captures-definition-scope semantic is verified at M3 via
#   tests/chk/closure/counter.chk (counter increments outer n correctly).
#   Compound assignment (i += x) is also not yet supported at M3.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with prototype slot assignment):
# # var i = 41; [00000001] 41
# # var Object.f = function(x) { i += x } | {};
# # { var i = 0; Object.f(1) };
# # [00000002:error] !!! input.u:4.31: lookup failed: i
# # i; [00000004] 41
